<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9092" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">collŏcātĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conl-</span></b> ),
			ōnis, f.
		colloco, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a putting together</i>, <i>arrangement</i>, <i>a setting up</i>, <i>erecting</i>, <i>placing</i>, <i>collocation</i> (except in rhet. use, very rare).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">siderum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Univ. 9, 26</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">moenium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr. 5,
					3</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> Esp.
			in speech: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">verborum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 3, 43, 171</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">2, 13, 54</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Or. 25,
				83</span></i>; <i><span class="en">70, 232</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 1,
				10, 22</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">id. 8</span></i>, prooem. § 6; 8, 3,
			41; 9, 4, 58; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">9, 4, 89: argumentorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 2, 42, 181</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rerum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint.
					3, 3, 8</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Esp.: filiae, <i>an endowing</i>, <i>giving in marriage</i> (v. colloco, I. B.), <i><span class="en">Cic. Clu.
				66, 190</span></i>.</div>
